From: kusti420 <virtuaalnepannkook@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] usb: gadget: uvc: queue whole 1080p frames of bright scenes, 128 requests by default

0012 queues each frame in one go with up to 64 requests (3 x 1024-byte
payloads at high speed, 192 KiB). 1080p MJPEG frames of a bright, detailed
scene are 150-200 KiB: 54 payloads median, 67 at most in the measured
streams, so some of them are larger than the request pool. The rest of
those frames is continued from the completion handler, one request per
completion, with 63 requests (7.9 ms) queued ahead.

The dwc3 bottom half (dwc3_bh_work on the unbound WQ_HIGHPRI ordered
workqueue dwc_wq, a CFS kworker) handles events late now and then. Measured
with ftrace (dwc3_event Transfer In Progress against the microframe of its
TRB) over 3 minutes of 1080p streaming: p99 1.6 ms, p99.9 3.6 ms, worst
5.9 ms; another run had 7.6 ms. That is within a few hundred microseconds
of the 7.9 ms margin. A refill that comes later than that is past its
interval and is missed.

Default to 128 requests (384 KiB, module parameter usb_f_uvc.num_requests,
4..192), so that a whole frame is queued up front and none of its payloads
depends on completion latency. The dwc3 ring has 255 usable TRBs, so 128
requests plus an error payload fit. Queueing 128 requests takes about
0.45 ms (3.4 us per request measured), well inside the 16 microframes
(2 ms) before dwc3 starts the transfer.

Used by MonsterROM target/a52sxq/patches/usb_webcam (on top of 0012).
---
diff --git a/drivers/usb/gadget/function/uvc.h b/drivers/usb/gadget/function/uvc.h
--- a/drivers/usb/gadget/function/uvc.h
+++ b/drivers/usb/gadget/function/uvc.h
@@ -68,7 +68,8 @@
  */
 
 #define UVC_MIN_NUM_REQUESTS			4
-#define UVC_MAX_NUM_REQUESTS			64
+#define UVC_MAX_NUM_REQUESTS			192
+#define UVC_DEF_NUM_REQUESTS			128
 #define UVC_MAX_REQUEST_SIZE			64
 #define UVC_MAX_EVENTS				4
 
diff --git a/drivers/usb/gadget/function/uvc_video.c b/drivers/usb/gadget/function/uvc_video.c
--- a/drivers/usb/gadget/function/uvc_video.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/gadget/function/uvc_video.c
@@ -23,14 +23,16 @@
 
 /*
  * Number of USB requests per stream. With high-bandwidth isochronous
- * endpoints (3 x 1024 bytes per microframe) 64 requests hold 192 KiB, i.e. a
- * whole MJPEG frame is handed to the controller at once and the controller
- * has several milliseconds of data queued while the completion handler
- * refills it. Read when the stream is enabled.
+ * endpoints (3 x 1024 bytes per microframe) 128 requests hold 384 KiB, i.e.
+ * a whole MJPEG frame is handed to the controller at once (1080p frames of
+ * bright, detailed scenes reach 200 KiB, 67 payloads), so no payload of it
+ * depends on how fast completions are handled. Larger frames are continued
+ * from the completion handler, with num_requests - 1 requests queued ahead.
+ * Read when the stream is enabled.
  */
-static unsigned int uvc_num_requests = UVC_MAX_NUM_REQUESTS;
+static unsigned int uvc_num_requests = UVC_DEF_NUM_REQUESTS;
 module_param_named(num_requests, uvc_num_requests, uint, 0644);
-MODULE_PARM_DESC(num_requests, "USB requests per video stream (4-64)");
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(num_requests, "USB requests per video stream (4-192)");
 
 /*
  * Diagnostics only: with drop_missed=0, a frame that lost a payload to a
